1. UNOFFICIAL — NO AFFILIATION

   This is UNOFFICIAL software, NOT affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported
   by FranklinWH. It interfaces with the aGate over the standard SunSpec Modbus
   TCP API, including undocumented FranklinWH extension registers (the 15500+
   range) that are outside SunSpec conformance. Either may change, break, or
   become unavailable without notice.

   FranklinWH, aGate and aPower are trademarks of their respective owners, used
   here only to describe what this Software communicates with.

   Do NOT contact FranklinWH support about this Software. Raise issues, defects
   or feature requests at:
   https://github.com/david2069/franklinwh-modbus-bridge/issues

2. COMPLIANCE & ANTI-CIRCUMVENTION

   This Software issues WRITE commands to grid-connected battery hardware. It
   can change operating mode, reserve state of charge, and charge/discharge
   power, and can schedule those changes unattended.

   You are responsible for keeping your gateway and battery settings, controls
   and operation compliant with the configuration set through the official
   FranklinWH mobile app and the installer/support portal.

   FranklinWH-managed settings may exist to, among other things:
     - protect the safety and longevity of the battery and gateway;
     - apply software updates and restrict your ability to view or change
       battery, grid-import or grid-export controls;
     - enforce your local electricity grid profile and any import/export limits
       or prohibitions;
     - enforce restrictions tied to contractual incentives, subsidies, or
       VPP/grid programmes.

   If you use this Software to bypass or override any such control, restriction
   or compliance measure — deliberately or inadvertently — you do so entirely at
   your own risk. This is neither condoned nor encouraged by the authors.

3. CONFORMANCE REFERENCES

   FranklinWH's SunSpec Modbus conformance is published by the SunSpec Alliance
   as document SM-000028:
     - Modbus PICS (Protocol Implementation Conformance Statement):
       https://sunspec.org/wp-content/uploads/2009/03/UPDATED_FranklinWH_Modbus_PICS_SM-000028.xlsx
     - IEEE 1547 certificate:
       https://sunspec.org/wp-content/uploads/2009/03/UPDATED_FranklinWH_Modbus_1547_Certificate_SM-000028.pdf

   The PICS is the authority for which models and points a firmware is certified
   for. The 15500+ extension registers are NOT SunSpec and fall outside it;
   their behaviour is documented in docs/vendor-issues.md from observation, not
   from a specification.
